#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:5
#: 8caaa1cd596043ab81c67a595baf6b2f
msgid "Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:9
#: 9eebde910573441194fa7fbd9cc85555
msgid "Simulation allows for the safe testing of experimental code and settings. Crashing virtual vehicles is a lot cheaper than crashing real ones!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:12
#: fafff486498642b4b76ebdbf545b1c23
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:14
#: 929d599e049446a6b7a49970592939f5
msgid "Simulation is implemented by using a Flight Dynamics Model (FDM) of the vehicle to simulate the physics involved with vehicle movement. It receives inputs from a SITL (Software in the Loop) program running the ArduPilot firmware (which are the firmware's servo/motor outputs) and outputs vehicle status,position, velocities, etc. that result from those inputs back to the firmware simulation. Just as sensors would in the real world case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:16
#: bc072f401d5d4f2690325b90ff4f364d
msgid "Pilot control is implemented either by joystick, dedicated simulation controller box(like Interlink), or by MAVLink commands from a Ground Control Station program (GCS), like MAVProxy or Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:18
#: febd1e0310034bd2ae4e7e48845c9504
msgid "This is illustrated below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:22
#: 0863bba5d4ec4f6dbc7bea2823558c1d
msgid "ArduPilot provides a native firmware simulator + FDM program (all launched by sim_vehicle.py), often simply referred to as ``SITL``, which is usually used with its developer GCS, MAVProxy. ArduPilot's firmware simulator and FDM can also be used by Mission Planner for SITL simulations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:24
#: 463961bf546b46bd9f05d0f69fd8656d
msgid "In addition, the ArduPilot firmware simulator element can also be interfaced to other FDM/Graphics programs that are normally used as stand-alone flight/vehicle simulators in order to get more realistic physics models and/or high definition vehicle graphics, such as RealFlight or X-Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:28
#: 0f36eb7f937f40129e62d7aebd9610e4
msgid "For code developers, we recommend starting with ArduPilot's native :ref:`Software In The Loop (SITL) <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` because the setup is easiest, it does not require a flight controller, and all vehicle types are supported. For non-developers, using Mission Planners integrated simulator does not require setting up a code building environment, for those only wishing to explore simulated behavior of vehicles using existing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:30
#: 21ae2c9520514ddd999d83ffde1fec40
msgid "The most commonly used simulators are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:32
#: 6d2b6b1360354507976be69dd6787caa
msgid ":ref:`SITL (Software In The Loop) <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` is the simulator most commonly used by developers. It is a simple simulator that is built within all SITL builds of ArduPilot. It is used by the :ref:`autotester <the-ardupilot-autotest-framework>` and other simulators below are actually built on top of SITL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:33
#: a42d59a59ded436cbf3b4cb3307dbe3f
msgid ":ref:`Mission Planner <planner:mission-planner-simulation>` can be used in Windows to simulate with Mission Planner as GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:34
#: 82ef296d40cb44d2905f9437e0e51e6e
msgid ":ref:`Gazebo <sitl-with-gazebo>` is the official DARPA virtual robotics simulator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:35
#: 1cb6c9fc4eeb4272b9882046b4156058
msgid ":ref:`XPlane-10 <sitl-with-xplane>` a commercial flight simulator with a rich 3D interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:36
#: 3dfd072aeae14959b45f041521be790e
msgid ":ref:`XPlane-10 Soaring<soaring-sitl-with-xplane>` soaring on XPlane-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:37
#: 7a91f0d4ab0e413882530325121c6a14
msgid ":ref:`RealFlight <sitl-with-realflight>` a commercial flight simulator with a rich 3D interface and ability to design custom vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:38
#: 5e2481e3cbd44aab917e9dee3ade9e9b
msgid ":ref:`Morse <sitl-with-morse>` a robotics simulation environment commonly used in research"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:39
#: 0af17876cd2242bea17add703ac8eb3a
msgid ":ref:`Replay <testing-with-replay>` has no graphical interface but allows re-running master from a dataflash log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:40
#: ca0c4c5116074b31ba63e7e1ddd353ea
msgid ":ref:`JSBSim <sitl-with-jsbsim>` is a sophisticated open-source plane and multicopter simulator with no graphical interface. It can be used with a wide variety of airframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:41
#: 69a2834e23ca44fabb7e9158e20ddcae
msgid ":ref:`AirSim <sitl-with-airsim>` is an open-source, cross-platform simulator for drones & cars, built on Unreal Engine for physically and visually realistic simulations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:42
#: b88040070f644406b731da9fa2f597bd
msgid ":ref:`Silent Wings Soaring<soaring-sitl-with-silentwings>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:43
#: 677911b6526e4dd39db633e6a9eeaa6e
msgid ":ref:`MATLAB and Simulink<sitl-with-MATLAB>` are numerical computing environments used for developing algorithms and plotting data developed by `MathWorks <https://www.mathworks.com/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:44
#: d6b788f442b54de6b0009dcf03fd41a5
msgid ":ref:`JSON interface<sitl-with-JSON>` The JSON interface is a generic interface protocol designed to be easy to implement for those developing physics backend. There are Python and MATLAB examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:45
#: aad3a52c1735414b9fdf527a0f1734f7
msgid ":ref:`Webots <sitl-with-webots>` is a cross-platform robotics simulator that is quick to set up and get running. It currently has examples for multicopter and rover vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:48
#: b0326ef5157143a8bf63ce75e22cfa21
msgid "Less often used simulators include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:50
#: fef95fd7ee6040c58b83097c4a20e1d5
msgid ":ref:`Last Letter <using-last_letter-as-an-external-sitl-simulator>` is a simpler simulator (fixed wing only) with lower CPU requirements than most other simulators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:51
#: 3c6cb65f16fb4a769d99a80e0b0cf55f
msgid ":ref:`CRRCSim <simulation-2sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loopusing-using-the-crrcsim-simulator>` is a less commonly used simulator for fixed wing and helicopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simulation-2.rst:52
#: b5f90ceec3f645c5b85c6499990ccbf8
msgid ":ref:`SCRIMMAGE <sitl-with-scrimmage>` is an open-source vehicle simulator focused on collaborative robotics"
msgstr ""

